# START — Agent Entry Gate & Routing Specification
Floor: 2
Thrust: 9
Patch: 0
File: openOODA/START.oot

Operate within this directory. All relative paths start from this directory.

## 0. The 6 Strategic Pillars & Core Laws

1. Pillar 1 (First Principles): Derive from IEEE 754, NIST KATs, RFCs. Reject incomplete stubs.
2. Pillar 2 (Boyd's E-M Engine): Ps = ((T - D) / W) * V. Maximize emission speed, eliminate GC/drag, minimize context/token weight.
3. Pillar 3 (Negative Trust & Red Team): Assume unverified code is defective. Multi-agent teams must deploy 4 Adversarial Red Team auditors with veto power (see REDTEAM.oot for Negative-Trust Doctrine & 4 Red Team roles):
   - Red 1 (Heuristic Hunter): Probes lowering to reject token/string bag-of-words heuristics.
   - Red 2 (Boundary Falsifier): Probes validators with dynamic oversized inputs (e.g. head_dim = 512).
   - Red 3 (Data-Path Tracer): Rejects (void)code and silent fallback routing (k_main -> vec-add).
   - Red 4 (Hermetic Jailor): Rejects out-of-tree escapes and parent directory lookups.
4. Pillar 4 (80/20 Leverage): Focus on SSA mem2reg, flat closures, 256-bit SIMD (f32x8, f64x4, fma), direct ELF64/WASM emission, linear arenas.
5. Pillar 5 (Capability Security): Zero ambient authority with 14 unforgeable capability tokens.
6. Pillar 6 (Generational Stratification): Treat Gen 1-4 as deterministic libraries. Maintain continuous disk awareness.
7. Law 7 (File Extensions): Pure .oo (code) and .oot (docs). Prohibit .py, .js, .ts, .md in product code.
8. Law 8 (Hard Engineering): Build real AST pipelines. Decompose across modular files (<= 256 lines). Break-test first.
9. Law 9 (SemVer): v<Floor>.<Thrust>.<Patch>. Verified state: v2.9.0.

## 1. The 13 Canonical Process Boards
1. START.oot (Entry/Routing)    5. ROADMAP.oot (Active Sprint)  9. WORKFLOW.oot (OODA/Protocols)
2. RULES.oot (Laws/Axioms)      6. SHIPPED.oot (Capabilities)   10. QUICKREF.oot (Syntax/Types)
3. NORTHSTAR.oot (Architecture) 7. FORMAT.oot (Headers/Limits)  11. CONSTRAINTS.oot (Invariants/Bans)
4. MOONSHOTS.oot (Long-term)    8. SECURITY.oot (Capabilities)  12. STRUCTURE_EM.oot (E-M/Topology)
13. REDTEAM.oot (Adversarial/Veto)

## 2. Reading Priority (Token-Optimized)
- Always Read: User request, RULES.oot, SHIPPED.oot, SECURITY.oot §1-2, WORKFLOW.oot §0.
- When Coding: ROADMAP.oot, target RFC, CONSTRAINTS.oot.
- Only as Needed: FORMAT.oot (headers), QUICKREF.oot (syntax), MOONSHOTS.oot (specs).

## 3. Pre-Modification & Completion Gate
Before modifying product code, declare:
1. Active Goal (ROADMAP milestone).
2. Governing Axiom (RULES.oot principle).
3. Adversarial Break-Test (hostile probe that fails closed on current code).
Before claiming victory: Execute all 4 Red Team falsification probes live (per 4-Gate Blocking Veto Protocol in REDTEAM.oot). If any facade is found, victory is vetoed.
